# EXAMPLE ONLY — the claude-sandbox launcher never reads this file.
#
# `claude-sandbox init` seeds .claude-sandbox/env.example; it never creates a
# real .claude-sandbox/env. Where to put variables:
#
#   - Shared secrets (API tokens, webhooks) belong in an UPSTREAM env, e.g.
#     <workspace>/.claude-sandbox/env in a parent directory. Every project
#     below it inherits them, and refreshing a token there reaches them all.
#   - Copy this file to .claude-sandbox/env (next to it) ONLY for a genuine
#     per-project override. Keys in a project env OVERRIDE the same keys
#     upstream — a stale token copied here silently hides the fresh one.
#
# The launcher passes every .claude-sandbox/env found from the filesystem root
# down to the project as stacked `docker run --env-file` flags: LATER (more
# local) files override earlier ones for duplicate keys.
#
# Syntax: KEY=value, one per line. Blank lines and #-comments are the only
# special syntax. Do NOT quote values — `docker --env-file` does no quote
# stripping and no variable expansion, so QUOTES BECOME PART OF THE VALUE
# (a quoted API token stays set and non-empty but fails auth). The launcher
# warns at startup if it spots a quoted value.
#
# This example holds no secrets and may be committed. A real
# .claude-sandbox/env is gitignored — never commit it.

# Discord webhook for MCP notification server
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/YOUR_ID/YOUR_TOKEN

# Discord webhook for Claude Code notification hooks (permission prompts, idle)
# CLAUDE_NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/YOUR_ID/YOUR_TOKEN
